    <summary>A free, open source web browser for Windows: a column of tabs, spaces, Chrome extensions, ads and trackers blocked. An unofficial port of Search.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Oriel brings the design of Search, the small fast browser for the Mac by Office Commun, to Windows: a column of tabs down the left (or a strip across the top), one field for addresses and searches, and the page as a card beside them.

* Spaces and pinned tabs, Split View, reading mode, translation on your PC.
* Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store.
* Ads and trackers blocked with uBlock Origin's lists, in the network layer.
* Passwords behind Windows Hello; import from Chrome, Edge, Brave, Opera and Arc.
* Free, open source (MIT). No account and no telemetry.

Oriel is built on Chromium through Electron. It is **not affiliated with or endorsed by** Office Commun.

## Package notes

* The installer is Oriel's own (NSIS), run silently for the current user; Chocolatey checks its SHA-256 against the one in this package, which is the one in `SHA256SUMS.txt` on the release.
* Oriel isn't code-signed yet, so Windows may ask before it runs.
* Oriel updates itself once installed. `choco upgrade oriel` follows the releases too.
* x64 and ARM64 are both supported.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/carpaaaaa/oriel/releases/tag/v0.1.11</releaseNotes>
